\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A unit partition with a nonunit marginal}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{Take one vertex and a loop edge. Declare one face traversing this
loop once. Over #{k=\mathbb Z/4\mathbb Z} take the two-element group
#{G=\{1,-1\}}, acting trivially on #{k}, with the one-point scalar
orbit of #{1}. Set the edge and site factors to #{1}. The face
function has values #{1} at the identity and #{2} at the other group
element. Both conjugacy classes are singletons. The two
[connection marginal weights](fdip-010E) are #{1} and #{2}.
Their sum #{3} is a unit, with inverse #{3}. For the nonidentity
link the conditional quotient would require division by #{2}, which
has no inverse in #{k}. The unnormalized sum at this link is still
defined.}
